+## Scores and prizes
+
+Quiz **Settings** include **Number of winners** (a positive integer, default 3).
+Each game snapshots this setting along with its questions. Each correct last
+pick earns one point; tied scores rank by the total response time of correct
+answers, measured on the server from question opening to the last pick.
+No points are shown to players until **End quiz**.
+
+The big screen then shows the ordered leaderboard, and each phone shows its
+place and points. **Top N** awards prizes in leaderboard order. **Draw** preserves
+players above the cutoff score and randomly fills remaining prizes from everyone
+tied on that score, ignoring speed. Each click draws afresh and may repeat the
+previous outcome. Zero-point players never win. **Reset winners** clears prizes.
+Winner marks and **You won!** update live, including on already-ended screens.
+See [prize design notes](docs/prizes.md) for persistence and timing details.
+
